        {
            "block_label": "header",
            "block_content": "Style: Lessons in Clarity and Grace",
            "block_bbox": [
                164,
                70,
                420,
                91
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": null,
            "group_id": 1,
            "global_block_id": 1,
            "global_group_id": 1,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    164.0,
                    70.0
                ],
                [
                    419.0,
                    70.0
                ],
                [
                    419.0,
                    90.0
                ],
                [
                    164.0,
                    90.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Honest writers sometimes think they don’t have to worry about plagiarism. But even honest writers can plagiarize inadvertently, and even inadvertent plagiarism can damage a writer’s credibility and reputation or bring disciplinary consequences. Yet just as you can’t write well if, with every word you set down, you worry about violating some rule of correctness, so you can’t write well if, with every source you use, you worry about committing an act of plagiarism. You need to fear plagiarizing only if you fail to understand and follow reliable practices that ensure you will avoid it.",
            "block_bbox": [
                90,
                118,
                784,
                322
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 2,
            "global_block_id": 2,
            "global_group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    90.0,
                    118.0
                ],
                [
                    784.0,
                    118.0
                ],
                [
                    784.0,
                    322.0
                ],
                [
                    90.0,
                    322.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Plagiarists steal more than words: they steal the respect and recognition due to others for their work. And student plagiarists also steal acknowledgment and even grades due to their peers by making their peers' work seem worse in comparison to their own. When such theft becomes common, the community grows suspicious, then distrustful, then cynical: So who cares? Everyone does it. Teachers then must concern themselves less with teaching and learning and more with detecting dishonesty. Those who plagiarize thus fray the ethical fabric of their academic or professional communities.",
            "block_bbox": [
                90,
                325,
                785,
                530
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 3,
            "global_block_id": 3,
            "global_group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    90.0,
                    325.0
                ],
                [
                    785.0,
                    325.0
                ],
                [
                    785.0,
                    530.0
                ],
                [
                    90.0,
                    530.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The overriding principle is this: avoid doing anything that might lead an informed reader to think that you are taking credit for words or ideas that are not your own. This principle applies to sources of any kind: print, online, recorded, or oral. Some writers think that if something is freely circulated online, they are free to treat it as their own. They are wrong: cite everything you borrow.",
            "block_bbox": [
                90,
                533,
                784,
                660
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 4,
            "global_block_id": 4,
            "global_group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    90.0,
                    533.0
                ],
                [
                    784.0,
                    533.0
                ],
                [
                    784.0,
                    660.0
                ],
                [
                    90.0,
                    660.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "In particular, follow these practices:",
            "block_bbox": [
                127,
                664,
                435,
                687
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 5,
            "global_block_id": 5,
            "global_group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    127.0,
                    664.0
                ],
                [
                    435.0,
                    664.0
                ],
                [
                    435.0,
                    687.0
                ],
                [
                    127.0,
                    687.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. When you quote from a source: cite the source according to the conventions of your field, and put those words in quotation marks or in a block quotation.",
            "block_bbox": [
                91,
                701,
                783,
                778
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 6,
            "global_block_id": 6,
            "global_group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    91.0,
                    701.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    701.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    778.0
                ],
                [
                    91.0,
                    778.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "2. When you paraphrase a passage from a source: cite the source according to the conventions of your field, and recast the passage entirely in your own words and in a new sentence structure.",
            "block_bbox": [
                90,
                791,
                784,
                867
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 7,
            "global_block_id": 7,
            "global_group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    90.0,
                    791.0
                ],
                [
                    784.0,
                    791.0
                ],
                [
                    784.0,
                    867.0
                ],
                [
                    90.0,
                    867.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "3. When you use an idea or method you found in a source: cite the source according to the conventions of your field. If the entire source concerns the idea or method, do not add page numbers.",
            "block_bbox": [
                91,
                881,
                783,
                958
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 8,
            "global_block_id": 8,
            "global_group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    91.0,
                    881.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    881.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    958.0
                ],
                [
                    91.0,
                    958.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Of course, you can't follow these good practices if you take sloppy notes or if you don't know how to properly quote from and cite your sources.",
            "block_bbox": [
                90,
                971,
                783,
                1022
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 9,
            "global_block_id": 9,
            "global_group_id": 9,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    90.0,
                    971.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    971.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    1022.0
                ],
                [
                    90.0,
                    1022.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Taking Good Notes",
            "block_bbox": [
                92,
                1042,
                306,
                1069
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 9,
            "group_id": 10,
            "global_block_id": 10,
            "global_group_id": 10,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    92.0,
                    1042.0
                ],
                [
                    306.0,
                    1042.0
                ],
                [
                    306.0,
                    1069.0
                ],
                [
                    92.0,
                    1069.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "To use and cite sources appropriately, you must start by taking good notes. Since that work can be tedious, set up a system to get things right the first time so that you don't have to check and recheck, again and again.",
            "block_bbox": [
                90,
                1077,
                784,
                1154
            ],
            "block_id": 11,
            "block_order": 10,
            "group_id": 11,
            "global_block_id": 11,
            "global_group_id": 11,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    90.0,
                    1077.0
                ],
                [
                    784.0,
                    1077.0
                ],
                [
                    784.0,
                    1154.0
                ],
                [
                    90.0,
                    1154.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. Record bibliographical information the first time you touch a source. Do this early, not when you are rushing to meet a deadline.",
            "block_bbox": [
                91,
                1167,
                783,
                1217
            ],
